    "result": "Perfect! I've successfully added weekly subscription support to subtrack. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. **src/cycles.js** - Added weekly cycle support\n- Added `CYCLE.WEEK: 'weekly'` to the cycle types\n- Implemented monthly cost calculation for weekly plans: `price \u00d7 52 \u00f7 12` (rounded to nearest cent)\n- Implemented `nextCharge` for weekly plans: charges every 7 days from the start date\n\n### 2. **bin/subtrack.js** - CLI support for weekly subscriptions\n- Added `week` and `weekly` to the `EVERY` mapping for the `--every` flag\n- Updated `SHARE_PER_MONTH` to include weekly (52\u00f712 months)\n- Updated usage text to show `--every month|year|week`\n- Updated error message to mention week as an option\n\n### 3. **src/renewals.js** - Fixed renewal sorting\n- Changed sorting from shortLabel (which breaks across month boundaries) to actual date comparison\n- This ensures renewals are always listed chronologically\n\n### 4. **src/export.js** - Fixed CSV export for weekly plans\n- Updated to use `monthlyCents` function instead of hardcoded month mappings\n- Ensures weekly subscriptions are exported with correct monthly cost\n\n## Testing\n\nAll tests pass (34/34 \u2713). The implementation correctly:\n- Adds weekly subscriptions: `subtrack add \"Meal kit\" 59.90 --every week`\n- Calculates monthly costs: \u20ac59.90/week \u00d7 52 \u00f7 12 = \u20ac259.56/month\n- Schedules renewals every 7 days from the start date\n- Lists renewals chronologically\n- Exports CSV with correct values",
